      "description": "Sales Development Representative - London, England, United Kingdom | Careers - KMS Lighthouse Skip to content Our Solutions I Need Knowledge Management for My Call Center Cut call center holding times by 40% Help Center Unified Self-Service & Knowledge Experiences Onboarding & Training Cut onboarding and training times by up to 70% Field Service Reduce your field teams time-on-site by 60% Integrations Knowledge Center Blog Videos Events News Guides Webinars Reports Glossary ROI Calculator Case Studies About About us Careers Lighthouse University Contact us Book a Demo About The Position We are looking for a high-energy, driven professional with natural sales instincts to join our sales team! As part of the role, you will be based in central London, near Liverpool Street, Moorgate stations. Your role as a SAAS Sales Development Representative will be to hunt and close new business within the U.K & Europe for our SAAS Solutions products in Knowledge Management and AI Automation. Candidates should demonstrate their ability to grow activity and move things forward in order to advance in our organization. You will have the opportunity to join a company at the forefront of Customer Contact Solutions. With Fortune 500 customers, KMS Lighthouse is an industry leader and award-winning Knowledge Management company. This is the place to be if you're interested in combining technology, innovation, and sales. Responsibilities Prospecting for new clients. Cold calling, emailing, and developing new accounts are part of this process. Communicate effectively with new and existing leads. Prospecting for qualified sales opportunities. Conduct discovery sessions with clients to pass along to the Sales Executives. Track opportunities using the CRM and follow the sales process as directed by the Sales Executives. Create a pipeline of qualified opportunities. Develop a deep understanding of the KMS and related products. Establish a network of customers and accounts via CRM, LinkedIn, and networking events. A training program will be provided so that day-to-day responsibilities can be carried out. An understanding of HubSpot and Linkedin tools can be advantageous Requirements Experience in enterprise software is preferred, with 1-2 years of experience in lead generation. Prospecting for new business with proven success. Communicates effectively in both written and oral form. A strong presentation skill set. An attitude of self-starting, motivation, and drive. The ability to work in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment. The ability to multitask, take initiative, prioritize, and manage time effectively. Excellent written and verbal English skills Benefits Clear career progression path A commission-incentivized role Wage competitive with industry standards Fitness memberships Insurance for private healthcare Apply for this job Our Solutions Call Center Help Center Self Service Field Service Onboarding & Training Integrations Azure OpenAI Integration Salesforce Integration Genesys Integration Zendesk Integration Freshworks Integration Dynamic 365 Integration Microsoft Teams Integration AWS Integration Knowledge Center Blog Videos Events News Guides Webinars Reports Glossary Case Studies ROI Calculator About Book a Demo Lighthouse University Careers Contact us Social LinkedIn YouTube Terms and Privacy Policy Modern Day Slavery Policy KMS Lighthouse Application Privacy Policy Environmental, Social and Governance Policy KMS Lighthouse Application Terms of Use Accessibility Toolbar close Toggle the visibility of the Accessibility Toolbar keyboard Keyboard Navigation visibility_off Disable Animations nights_stay Contrast format_size Increase Text text_fields Decrease Text font_download Readable Font title Mark Titles link Highlight Links & Buttons Powered with favorite Love by Codenroll",
