      "title": "Support Engineer Team Lead",
      "location": null,
      "url": "https://kmslh.com/careers/co/dallas-texas-united-states/4F.27D/support-engineer-team-lead/all/",
      "description": "Support Engineer Team Lead - Dallas, Texas, United States | Careers - KMS Lighthouse Skip to content Our Solutions I Need Knowledge Management for My Call Center Cut call center holding times by 40% Help Center Unified Self-Service & Knowledge Experiences Onboarding & Training Cut onboarding and training times by up to 70% Field Service Reduce your field teams time-on-site by 60% Integrations Knowledge Center Blog Videos Events News Guides Webinars Reports Glossary ROI Calculator Case Studies About About us Careers Lighthouse University Contact us Book a Demo About The Position KMS Lighthouse is one of the hottest up and coming tech companies working with Fortune 500 and Fortune 1000 enterprises around the world! Named the #1 knowledge management company in the Forrester Wave Report 2024, we are an industry leader in knowledge management solutions. We are looking for a Support Engineer Team Lead to function as a player-coach - supporting our SaaS knowledge management system and leading a 3-person team in day-to-day work life. You will work closely with the Global Head of Support, DevOps, and Development teams to lead the support team and represent KMS Lighthouse as a professional and technical authority for clients. The lead in this role must be able to take initiative and effectively communicate with their team, senior leadership, and clients. Responsibilities Function as the primary technical team player-coach Lead the support team in day-to-day operations Screen incoming tickets, distribute them to specialized team members, and work on tickets Provide a high level of troubleshooting for our major clients in North America and around the Globe Interface with clients regularly whether for live troubleshooting, various technical calls, and/or escalations Troubleshoot incidents and system events; escalating to specialized teams when necessary Work closely with development teams and DevOps teams Take an active role in the customer lifecycle and business continuity events Train, mentor, and develop the support team (i.e. skill development, professional development, etc.) Requirements 3 years of experience as a Support Engineer or in a similarly technical role 1 year of experience leading a team Must have experience interfacing with clients, preferably enterprise clients Experience directly supporting a SaaS solution is required Experience with Linux administration and scripting is required Experience working with Microsoft Azure or other cloud providers Experience working with Virtualization systems (VMware or other) Experience working with Kubernetes Knowledge of Windows administration Benefits Medical, Dental, Vision 401K & 401K Match PTO & Sick Days 11 Paid Holidays Apply for this job Our Solutions Call Center Help Center Self Service Field Service Onboarding & Training Integrations Azure OpenAI Integration Salesforce Integration Genesys Integration Zendesk Integration Freshworks Integration Dynamic 365 Integration Microsoft Teams Integration AWS Integration Knowledge Center Blog Videos Events News Guides Webinars Reports Glossary Case Studies ROI Calculator About Book a Demo Lighthouse University Careers Contact us Social LinkedIn YouTube Terms and Privacy Policy Modern Day Slavery Policy KMS Lighthouse Application Privacy Policy Environmental, Social and Governance Policy KMS Lighthouse Application Terms of Use Accessibility Toolbar close Toggle the visibility of the Accessibility Toolbar keyboard Keyboard Navigation visibility_off Disable Animations nights_stay Contrast format_size Increase Text text_fields Decrease Text font_download Readable Font title Mark Titles link Highlight Links & Buttons Powered with favorite Love by Codenroll",
